{"name":"Cherry Tree","hex":"#dfb7b4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Cherry Tree","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A suburb of Livesey parish, Blackburn with Darwen district, Lancashire, England .","A suburb of Romiley, Stockport borough, Greater Manchester, England ."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Cherry_Tree"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cherry","blocks":[{"text":"A cherry is the fruit of many plants of the genus Prunus, and is a fleshy drupe."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Cherry_season_%2848216568227%29.jpg/330px-Cherry_season_%2848216568227%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cherry"},{"title":"Cherry blossom","blocks":[{"text":"The cherry blossom, or sakura, is the flower of trees in Prunus subgenus Cerasus. Sakura usually refers to flowers of ornamental cherry trees, such as cultivars of Prunus serrulata, not trees grown for their fruit. Cherry blossoms have been described as having a vanilla-like smell, which is mainly attributed to coumarin."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Sakura_and_Moss_Pink_-_%E6%A1%9C%28%E3%81%95%E3%81%8F%E3%82%89%29%E3%81%A8%E8%8A%9D%E6%A1%9C%28%E3%81%97%E3%81%B0%E3%81%96%E3%81%8F%E3%82%89%29.jpg/330px-Sakura_and_Moss_Pink_-_%E6%A1%9C%28%E3%81%95%E3%81%8F%E3%82%89%29%E3%81%A8%E8%8A%9D%E6%A1%9C%28%E3%81%97%E3%81%B0%E3%81%96%E3%81%8F%E3%82%89%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cherry_blossom"},{"title":"Cherry Tree (EP)","blocks":[{"text":"Cherry Tree is an EP by the American indie rock band the National, released in July 2004. It was reissued on June 28, 2011, by Brassland Records, the same label on which it was initially published."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c0/Cherry_Tree_%28EP%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campai